    "_features_S1_note": "21 nodes = the 30-node ak8_gpt_* set (all minus the 3 parent sums topbw/topw/qcd) with the 10 leptonic top/W-decay categories merged into one ak8_gpt_lepq = their sum. These are mutually-exclusive sub-classes of one GloParT parent softmax (leptonic top-or-W decay), so the sum is a lossless union probability, not a dropped feature -- and all 10 individually contributed <0.0012 permutation AUC (9 of 10 below 0.001; physically expected since our AK8 jet is a hadronic W->cb candidate). cc/qcdbb/qcdcc/topbwcs/qq/ss/tauhtauh were also individually <0.001 but are NOT merged: they are physically distinct categories (not mutually-exclusive sub-classes of one summed parent), so low permutation importance there means 'not needed for this S:B split', not 'redundant' -- kept as-is per instruction.",
